<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Cuban Revolutionary Party</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1892–1898</span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Cuban Revolutionary Party was founded in 1892 by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jose-marti">José Martí</a> among Cuban and Puerto Rican exiles in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a> to prepare and finance a war for the independence of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cuba">Cuba</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/puerto-rico">Puerto Rico</a>. It organised the uprising of February 1895 and represented the rebels abroad. It was dissolved in 1898, after the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spanish-american-war">Spanish-American War</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/cuban-revolutionary-party.jpg" alt="Cuban Revolutionary Party" width="320" height="386" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Samhanin · CC BY 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Coat_of_arms_of_Cuba_(19th_century).svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
